cases.description:
The signature is presented over NON-canonical JSON: a pretty-printed, reordered, whitespace-laden serialization of the card instead of its JCS form. The base64url payload below decodes to '{
  "name": "AIGEN Protocol Agent",
  "url": "https://cryptogenesis.duckdns.org"
}'. Because the verifier recomputes JCS(card) for the signing input, a signature over any non-canonical encoding fails. This is the test that an implementation actually canonicalizes (rather than hashing whatever bytes it was handed).
